Two load-bearing contradictions are emerging. First, the governing document explicitly treats “a timer fires” as a host event that an adapter deposits, while the lease document forbids that route yet promises bounded judgment cadence. Second, DaoStream does not guarantee single-writer streams or author identity, so the lease’s ambient-authority premise is not granted by its substrate. I’m checking the remaining findings for exact corrective language and severity.
